        "Wudu is the spiritual and physical purification required before standing in prayer.\n\nThe Quran establishes four obligatory pillars (Fara'id) in Surah Al-Ma'idah (5:6):\n1. Washing the face from forehead to chin and ear to ear.\n2. Washing both arms including the elbows.\n3. Wiping at least a quarter of the head with wet hands (Hanafi; Sunnat is wiping the whole head).\n4. Washing both feet up to and including the ankles.\n\nProphetic Sunnahs (Recommended Practices):\n- Starting with Bismillah and intention (Niyyah) in the heart.\n- Washing the hands thrice up to wrists.\n- Rinsing the mouth (Madmadah) and cleaning the nose (Istinshaq) thrice.\n- Running wet fingers through the beard and between fingers and toes (Takhlil).\n- Maintaining sequential order (Tartib) without prolonged interruption (Muwalat)." to "Wudhu adalah penyucian rohani dan jasmani yang diperlukan sebelum berdiri dalam solat.\n\nAl-Quran menetapkan empat rukun wajib (Fara'id) dalam Surah Al-Ma'idah (5:6):\n1. Mencuci muka dari dahi ke dagu dan telinga ke telinga.\n2. Membasuh kedua belah tangan termasuk siku.\n3. Menyapu sekurang-kurangnya seperempat kepala dengan tangan yang basah (Hanafi; Sunat ialah menyapu seluruh kepala).\n4. Membasuh kedua-dua kaki sehingga dan termasuk buku lali.\n\nSunnah Nabawi (Amalan yang Disyorkan):\n- Bermula dengan Bismillah dan niat (Niyyah) dalam hati.\n- Mencuci tangan tiga kali sehingga pergelangan tangan.\n- Membilas mulut (Madmadah) dan membersihkan hidung (Istinshaq) tiga kali.\n- Menjalankan jari basah melalui janggut dan antara jari tangan dan kaki (Takhlil).\n- Mengekalkan susunan urutan (Tartib) tanpa gangguan yang berpanjangan (Muwalat).",
        "Khushu' is inner humility, stillness of the limbs, and attentive contemplation of what one is reciting.\n\nPractical Anchors for Khushu':\n- Prepare before the Takbir: Perform wudu mindfully, arrive before iqamah, and eliminate immediate physical distractions.\n- Contemplate the Words: Recite slowly (Tartil). When saying 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alameen', remember Allah responds directly: 'My servant has praised Me' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Fix the Gaze: Direct your gaze respectfully at the place of prostration (Sujud), rather than looking around.\n- Remember the Final Prayer: The Prophet (peace be upon him) advised: 'Pray as if it were your farewell prayer' (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171)." to "Khushu' adalah kerendahan hati, ketenangan anggota badan, dan renungan penuh perhatian terhadap apa yang dibaca.\n\nSauh Praktikal untuk Khushu':\n- Bersedia sebelum Takbir: Berwuduk dengan penuh kesedaran, tiba sebelum iqamah, dan hilangkan gangguan fizikal serta-merta.\n- Renung-renungkan Kata-kata: Lafaz perlahan-lahan (Tartil). Apabila mengucapkan 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alameen', ingatlah Allah menjawab secara langsung: 'Hamba-Ku telah memuji-Ku' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Betulkan Pandangan: Arahkan pandangan dengan hormat ke tempat sujud (Sujud), daripada melihat sekeliling.\n- Ingat Solat Akhir: Nabi (saw) berpesan: 'Solatlah seolah-olah solat perpisahan kamu' (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171).",
        "The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: 'Jibril kept enjoining good treatment of the neighbor upon me until I thought he would assign him a share of inheritance.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6014).\n\nIslamic teachings identify three classes of neighbors:\n1. A neighbor who is a relative and Muslim: has three rights (kinship, Islam, neighborhood).\n2. A neighbor who is Muslim: has two rights (Islam and neighborhood).\n3. A neighbor of different faith: has the sacred right of good neighborhood and kindness.\n\nHarm to neighbors is strictly condemned: 'By Allah he does not believe... whose neighbor is not safe from his harm.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6016)." to "Nabi Muhammad (saw) berkata: 'Jibril sentiasa mewasiatkan kepadaku supaya berbuat baik terhadap jiran sehingga aku menyangka dia akan memberikan bahagian pusaka kepadanya.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6014).\n\nAjaran Islam mengenal pasti tiga golongan jiran:\n1. Jiran yang kerabat dan Islam: mempunyai tiga hak (persaudaraan, Islam, kejiranan).\n2. Jiran yang beragama Islam: mempunyai dua hak (Islam dan kejiranan).\n3. Jiran yang berbeza kepercayaan: mempunyai hak suci kejiranan yang baik dan kebaikan.\n\nKemudaratan kepada jiran dikutuk dengan tegas: 'Demi Allah dia tidak beriman... yang jirannya tidak selamat dari bahayanya.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6016).",
